{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "metadata": {
    "id": "pw8-demo-node-delay",
    "name": "DEMO: NODE DELAY MULTI-TAP",
    "author": "Patchwork Eight Engineering",
    "description": "FX demo: NodeDelay (docs/FX_BANK.md 'ChowMatrix') -- a small delay-node TREE, not a single tap. Two root taps run in parallel straight off the input (parentIndex -1): node0 at 180ms panned hard left, node2 at 260ms panned center. Each root then feeds one CHILD node (parentIndex pointing at its parent): node1 (child of node0) adds another 140ms (320ms total from the original hit) panned hard right with some soft-clip distortion, and node3 (child of node2) adds 95ms (355ms total) panned left with lighter distortion. The result is an asymmetric, slightly-dirty cascade of echoes rather than a single evenly-spaced repeat -- structural per-node data (parentIndex/delayMs/feedback/pan/distortion/level per node), which is why this preset -- unlike the flat-parameter FX demos -- can only be built as a real .pw8 file, not via a plain VST3 parameter list.",
    "category": "pluck",
    "moods": ["fx-demo", "rhythmic", "asymmetric"],
    "genres": ["demo"],
    "tags": ["demo", "delay", "node-delay", "chowmatrix"],
    "createdAt": "2026-08-10T00:00:00Z",
    "engineVersion": "0.1.0",
